<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The rules screen: a modal canvas on the view of the table (a SceneView: a title, a pager, six lines of two rows, six rows of two
  items or two rows of fourteen tile pictures are up to 588 units, and the text needs 900 units of width, which a Screen canvas would
  not fit in a 480 px window at the user scale 1.5; it is text and pictures only, no touch target), shown by MahjongHudComponent exactly
  while MahjongGame::IsRulesOpen() (the Rules button of HudMenu). The component publishes rulesTitle, rulesPager, rulesLine0..5 and
  rulesItem0..11 from FormatRulesPage (Table/RulesText.h), sets the sprite of the pictures RulesTile0..27 (row r, tile c is r * 14 + c)
  and shows exactly the elements the page has: a hidden element takes no room in a stack, so the plate needs no fixed block heights. The
  plate is 588 units (32 padding + the blocks of a page and 8 between them, PageHeight in RulesText.h; a page that does not
  fit is split in two) and lies 40 units above the middle so that it ends clear of the bar RulesAction below it. The buttons are not in
  this canvas, they are in RulesAction: a control of a SceneView canvas is only 24 px high in the smallest window. A line is 48 units
  high (two rows of the 18 font are 47) and shrinks (AutoFit, down to 12) where a long line of a translation does not fit two rows in
  the narrowest windows (480 px wide), as the titles do; at the design size and in a window of 731 px no line is shrunk. The items (half a
  row, 28 high) shrink the same way: the portrait view is 720 wide and a window with side insets keeps 590 of it.
  In a narrow view (1080 x 768) 94% of the width is 1015, so maxWidth holds the plate to 960 (x 60..1020, y 50..638) and the pages fit as in
  landscape: no variant (MahjongRulesTest holds the matrix and the narrow windows).
  The page is laid out as a page, and no block grew for it: the Title is the heading band, the Pager a holder (28 high) of a small chip
  PagerChip (200 wide, raised, the text of rulesPager), a line a raised row of radius 8 (RulesLine<n>, 48 high) with a 4 wide accent bar
  (RulesLineBar<n>; the canvas has its own dim, so accent is allowed as on any modal) and the text in a child RulesLineText<n>, an item a
  raised chip of radius 8 (RulesItem<n>, half a row) with the text in RulesItemText<n>. A text component has no inset, so the air of a
  chip or a row is the margin of the child that holds the text, and the sizes of the blocks stay the constants of RulesText.h. A tile row
  is a recessed tray (surfaceDeep, radius 8) with a flex spacer at each end (RulesTrayLeft<r>, RulesTrayRight<r>: a stack has no main-axis
  centring) so the tiles, however many a page shows, stand in the middle side by side (no gap: 14 tiles and two gaps of 4 would not fit the narrowest window).
  Motion (UiPalette.h kMotion*): the canvas fades and rises from 0.96 over 0.18 s and leaves in 0.12 s; _transitionInput stays off: a click in the 0.18 s of the show is eaten, none of the choices here is worth a blind click, and a leaving modal frees the screen at once.
-->
